<title>USA: Northeast nuke outages cost $1.0 billion.</title>
<headline>Northeast nuke outages cost $1.0 billion.</headline>
<dateline>HARTFORD 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northeast Utilities estimates its past and projected nuclear power outage-related costs could reach almost $1 billion, Connecticut Attorney General Richard Blumenthal said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Blumenthal said Northeast made the estimation this week in a filing with the state Department of Public Utility Control (DPUC).</p>
<p>A Northeast spokesman was not immediately available for comment. The utility's three Millstone nuclear power plants in Waterford, Conn., have been closed for safety reasons since March 1996.</p>
